    pr_ref:  # 004c
    description: ""  # 004c
    fields:  # 004c
      statement: "rust.yaml rows std::process::exit and std::process::abort carry boundary subprocess. Source: abort() is one line calling crate::sys::abort_internal(), which on unix calls libc::abort() and raises SIGABRT on the CALLING process; exit() calls crate::rt::cleanup() then crate::sys::os::exit(code). Neither spawns a process, signals another process, nor exchanges data with one. The subprocess boundary asserts a crossing that does not occur."  # 004c
      root_cause: "Module-name attribution. Both live in std::process, whose other members (Command, Child) genuinely are subprocess primitives, so the boundary was applied at module granularity rather than per function."  # 004c
